WEBVTT

01:59.160 --> 02:01.079
Stand back, rookies.

02:01.830 --> 02:02.664
It's time...

02:04.582 --> 02:06.751
to show off our ODM gear.

02:09.295 --> 02:10.130
Let's go!

02:20.056 --> 02:23.852
2 HOURS EARLIER

02:27.438 --> 02:29.315
Looks like someone was here recently.

02:29.691 --> 02:31.442
It's odd for a place this near the wall.

02:32.152 --> 02:34.195
Some bandits probably used it as a base.

02:34.988 --> 02:37.824
It said, "Ruins of Utgard Castle"
on one of the signs.

02:38.700 --> 02:41.244
Who would have thought
there would be a castle around here?

02:43.329 --> 02:45.748
Hey, check it out. Look what I found.

02:46.207 --> 02:48.793
-Gelgar, is that booze I see?
-Yes.

02:50.628 --> 02:52.005
What the heck does it say?

02:52.297 --> 02:53.882
You're not going to drink it now, are you?

02:55.216 --> 02:57.510
Don't be stupid. Not at a time like this.

02:59.637 --> 03:03.558
How convenient. All this contraband
to enjoy for ourselves.

03:04.267 --> 03:07.353
Now you're making us sound like bandits.

03:09.105 --> 03:11.357
You rookies should try to get some rest.

03:11.900 --> 03:14.485
Titans won't be roaming about now,

03:15.111 --> 03:16.821
but the rest of us will take turns
keeping watch.

03:17.655 --> 03:19.991
We'll leave four hours before daybreak.

03:21.117 --> 03:22.035
Wait...

03:23.036 --> 03:26.372
What if the wall isn't broken after all?

03:26.789 --> 03:27.624
The Titans...

03:28.333 --> 03:30.668
where could they be invading from?

03:32.962 --> 03:34.464
Finding the answer to that...

03:35.215 --> 03:36.466
is our job for tomorrow.

03:40.428 --> 03:41.596
But what if...

03:41.846 --> 03:45.642
Maybe it's not nearly as bad
as we thought from the start.

03:48.019 --> 03:49.812
I'm just saying, but...

03:51.064 --> 03:53.983
Yes. There are barely any Titans
around here.

03:54.859 --> 03:56.945
If the wall really is broken, that is.

03:57.695 --> 04:01.449
The only group we saw
was during the initial sighting.

04:04.953 --> 04:06.871
Conny? What about your village?

04:07.622 --> 04:08.665
It was destroyed.

04:09.415 --> 04:11.376
Crushed to sticks and rubble
by the Titans.

04:13.628 --> 04:15.505
I see. How awful.

04:15.838 --> 04:17.131
But nobody there was eaten.

04:18.216 --> 04:21.970
I think they all escaped,
so there's that to be thankful for.

04:23.179 --> 04:24.722
Wasn't the village destroyed?

04:25.598 --> 04:29.602
The houses and stuff were wrecked,
but the villagers made it out safely.

04:30.270 --> 04:32.480
If anyone was eaten, then...

04:33.356 --> 04:35.316
there would've been blood and remains.

04:36.317 --> 04:39.821
But there wasn't any of that,
so it's the only explanation.

04:43.241 --> 04:46.202
Still, I can't stop thinking about it.

04:47.287 --> 04:48.830
There was that Titan at my house.

04:50.415 --> 04:55.003
It couldn't move on its own,
but it was lying right on top of my house.

04:56.546 --> 04:57.755
But it's weird...

04:58.589 --> 05:02.135
I don't know why,
but it reminded me of my mother...

05:03.469 --> 05:04.637
What does that--

05:04.721 --> 05:08.141
Conny, you're still saying that? You--

05:08.266 --> 05:09.392
What an idiot!

05:11.436 --> 05:13.980
Do you think your mother
might have been that Titan?

05:14.314 --> 05:17.025
Then how come you're so damn short?

05:17.317 --> 05:20.528
Come on, Conny! I knew you were stupid,

05:20.695 --> 05:23.156
but this is taking it to another level!

05:25.658 --> 05:29.120
Would you just shut up? This is absurd.

05:29.620 --> 05:31.497
If this theory of yours is correct,

05:31.789 --> 05:34.250
then that means your father
had to be a Titan, too.

05:34.751 --> 05:38.087
Otherwise, you know, they couldn't do it--

05:38.171 --> 05:40.590
Shut up! Go to sleep, you whore!

05:50.892 --> 05:52.894
What are you doing, Ymir?

05:53.478 --> 05:55.938
Prowling at night, Reiner?
Did you come to see me?

05:56.981 --> 05:58.066
I'm shocked.

05:58.483 --> 06:01.444
I was under the impression
that you had no interest in women.

06:02.111 --> 06:02.945
Yes.

06:03.321 --> 06:06.032
And it doesn't seem like
you have an interest in guys either.

06:08.117 --> 06:12.080
I thought I'd use this time to scavenge
for something that might fill my stomach.

06:12.747 --> 06:15.291
That'll probably end up
being my last meal.

06:17.752 --> 06:19.295
About Conny's village...

06:20.880 --> 06:23.049
Were you joking around on purpose?

06:24.425 --> 06:26.427
I'd appreciate it if you did more of that.

06:27.261 --> 06:30.598
So that he doesn't keep worrying
about his family.

06:31.265 --> 06:32.475
What are you talking about?

06:33.601 --> 06:37.146
This might do the trick.
Not that I like herring, but...

06:38.147 --> 06:40.191
Are there any more? Can I see it?

06:42.693 --> 06:43.569
Go for it.

06:45.696 --> 06:47.198
Canned food?

06:49.951 --> 06:51.828
What are these letters?

06:53.121 --> 06:54.413
I can't read any of it.

06:55.790 --> 06:57.375
This says herring on it?

07:00.044 --> 07:04.090
Are you able to read this language?

07:07.093 --> 07:09.303
Ymir, you're...

07:12.098 --> 07:13.141
Everyone, wake up!

07:13.599 --> 07:15.685
Get to the tower! Quickly!

07:19.689 --> 07:21.232
You've got to be freaking kidding me.

07:21.649 --> 07:24.110
I would be drinking right now
if it wasn't for you!

07:24.485 --> 07:26.237
This is all your fault!

07:28.406 --> 07:29.240
Let's go!

07:34.662 --> 07:37.874
Get your damn hands away from me!
You piece of shit!

07:50.678 --> 07:53.389
Look at that. Those little ones
got crushed by the fat one.

07:54.390 --> 07:55.433
Dumbasses.

07:56.642 --> 07:58.102
That was way too reckless!

07:58.394 --> 08:01.564
Couldn't you have avoided that
without wasting your blades?

08:02.023 --> 08:03.691
That's just how I do things.

08:04.066 --> 08:06.068
You better chalk that one up as an assist.

08:06.611 --> 08:08.112
How heroic of you.

08:09.238 --> 08:10.281
I'll think about it.

08:17.246 --> 08:19.248
I'm too late...

08:21.292 --> 08:22.710
The door is bashed in!

08:24.587 --> 08:25.796
The Titans broke through.

08:25.922 --> 08:28.424
Go back down and form
some sort of barricade.

08:28.799 --> 08:31.928
If you can't block them,
retreat back up here as a last resort.

08:32.887 --> 08:36.474
But that doesn't mean
we'll be able to help you.

08:38.226 --> 08:41.270
I'm not sure if we'll still be alive
if it comes to that.

08:42.313 --> 08:44.232
We've got to do what we're trained to do.

08:44.941 --> 08:48.027
Give it all we've got until we die!
Understand?

08:48.569 --> 08:49.487
-Got it!
-Got it!

08:52.657 --> 08:54.492
I'll go see how far they've come through!

08:55.243 --> 08:58.955
You guys grab boards or rods or whatever!
Bring everything you can carry!

08:59.580 --> 09:00.957
-Reiner!
-Hey!

09:01.999 --> 09:03.793
Wait up, Reiner! Hold on!

09:04.502 --> 09:07.755
Who does he think he is,
always taking the most dangerous job?

09:08.297 --> 09:09.257
Come on, man!

09:09.423 --> 09:11.592
Yes, that's a bad habit of his.

09:22.812 --> 09:23.813
They're still below.

09:26.941 --> 09:28.401
Well, it's still locked...

09:29.151 --> 09:33.114
But it's not like this old wooden door
will keep them out for long.

09:52.508 --> 09:53.801
They're here!

09:54.260 --> 09:56.178
Bring something, quick!

10:00.808 --> 10:01.767
Is this it?

10:02.852 --> 10:03.894
Will this be it?

10:05.438 --> 10:06.522
Is this the end?

10:21.162 --> 10:22.079
No...

10:22.913 --> 10:23.873
It can't be.

10:26.083 --> 10:27.335
I won't let it happen!

10:31.756 --> 10:33.215
I'm definitely going home!

10:34.467 --> 10:35.426
Reiner!

10:43.059 --> 10:44.518
Reiner, are you okay?

10:44.727 --> 10:45.686
Yes!

10:45.978 --> 10:48.272
Bertholdt, we're going to survive
and go home.

10:49.398 --> 10:51.275
We're going back to our hometown for sure.

10:51.942 --> 10:53.653
Right!

10:54.111 --> 10:54.945
We're going home!

10:55.988 --> 10:57.573
Reiner! Bertholdt!

10:58.824 --> 11:01.243
Hey, that's...
Do you have powder? A cannonball?

11:01.869 --> 11:04.413
Hell no! You'll just have to take
the whole thing!

11:04.830 --> 11:05.915
Out of the way!

11:24.183 --> 11:26.811
Looks like that worked out, miraculously.

11:27.269 --> 11:28.145
Yes.

11:28.354 --> 11:31.524
It's not getting up from that.
Not from one of that size.

11:31.941 --> 11:34.360
What now? All we have is this knife.

11:34.777 --> 11:35.861
Should I cut off its nape?

11:36.028 --> 11:36.987
Don't even try.

11:37.405 --> 11:38.989
You'll get hurt if it grabs you.

11:39.407 --> 11:42.827
For now, let's retreat back upstairs.

11:43.702 --> 11:46.372
There could be more than just one
that got inside.

11:51.335 --> 11:52.169
Conny!

11:59.844 --> 12:00.678
Reiner!

12:15.025 --> 12:16.152
Hey, Reiner...

12:18.195 --> 12:19.488
Don't tell me...

12:20.489 --> 12:22.324
You're going to jump out the window
with it?

12:22.616 --> 12:25.369
-I've got no other choice!
-Wait!

12:27.329 --> 12:29.832
If I could just slice open its jaw...

12:31.792 --> 12:32.710
You're free!

12:50.060 --> 12:52.146
What will we do if another comes through?

12:52.730 --> 12:55.691
We won't be lucky enough
to kill a second one.

12:55.941 --> 12:57.943
Yes, I'm with you there.

13:03.866 --> 13:05.618
Sorry. I'm sorry.

13:06.577 --> 13:08.078
I think it's broken.

13:08.454 --> 13:10.623
Yes, just my luck.

13:11.290 --> 13:13.292
We'll need a splint and a bandage.

13:13.959 --> 13:15.169
I know.

13:21.842 --> 13:22.676
Sorry...

13:25.346 --> 13:27.223
All I've got is this dirty cloth.

13:28.015 --> 13:28.849
Sorry.

13:30.643 --> 13:32.394
No, it helps.

13:33.437 --> 13:34.355
I've got to marry her.

13:35.105 --> 13:36.607
Are you all right, Reiner?

13:37.107 --> 13:38.692
Yes, I guess.

13:40.569 --> 13:41.570
By the way, Christa.

13:42.196 --> 13:44.031
My hand got scraped up a bit, too...

13:44.448 --> 13:46.700
What? Just spit on it or something.

13:48.494 --> 13:50.371
Sorry about that, Reiner.

13:51.622 --> 13:54.250
It seems like you're always saving my ass.

13:55.167 --> 13:58.170
Speaking of which,
Annie risked her life to save me, too.

13:59.171 --> 14:01.048
I've got to pay you back sometime.

14:01.799 --> 14:03.300
It's nothing, really...

14:05.177 --> 14:06.345
It's the normal thing to do.

14:07.846 --> 14:09.139
Because we're soldiers.

14:10.224 --> 14:11.433
I'm not so sure about that.

14:11.809 --> 14:13.435
I doubt I could ever be that brave.

14:14.562 --> 14:15.563
Hey, Bertholdt.

14:16.188 --> 14:18.023
Has Reiner always been like this?

14:19.316 --> 14:20.150
No.

14:20.442 --> 14:23.654
In the past, Reiner was more of a warrior.

14:25.447 --> 14:26.532
Unlike now.

14:28.158 --> 14:31.161
What does that mean?
What do you mean by "warrior"?

14:33.122 --> 14:36.458
For now, let's try to gather
anything useful we can find.

14:36.876 --> 14:39.837
That way, when we die,
we can do so without regrets.

14:42.047 --> 14:43.549
That's the Scouts for you...

14:44.300 --> 14:47.052
They're on a different level
from the other soldiers.

14:56.687 --> 14:58.522
That's mostly it for the big ones.

14:59.231 --> 15:00.733
Good thing we have this tower.

15:00.941 --> 15:03.277
Yes, we just might survive.

15:04.278 --> 15:06.405
-We'll go check on the recruits!
-Okay.

15:09.450 --> 15:10.284
What's that sound?

15:16.123 --> 15:16.957
The horses!

15:18.125 --> 15:18.959
What?

15:20.002 --> 15:20.836
Again?

15:21.462 --> 15:22.504
What's that sound?

15:28.886 --> 15:30.512
Lynne! Henning!

15:36.810 --> 15:37.770
What was that?

15:39.021 --> 15:41.315
It's no use. They both died instantly.

15:43.651 --> 15:44.818
This can't be...

15:46.236 --> 15:49.073
It's him! The one that walked off
towards the wall!

15:49.865 --> 15:51.742
That Beast Titan did this!

15:53.535 --> 15:56.497
A group of Titans approaching!
More than twice the number from earlier!

15:56.830 --> 15:57.790
What did you say?

15:58.332 --> 16:01.418
Their timing is too perfect,
like it's part of some strategy.

16:02.336 --> 16:03.295
I get the feeling...

16:04.046 --> 16:05.589
they've been toying with us
from the start.

16:34.493 --> 16:36.662
This is bad! I'm nearly out of gas!

16:43.377 --> 16:44.461
Did I get them?

16:53.804 --> 16:55.556
This tower won't hold for much longer.

16:56.390 --> 16:58.058
I only have a small amount of gas left.

16:58.642 --> 16:59.601
What about you?

17:00.102 --> 17:02.896
No gas here,
and I used up all of my blades.

17:03.897 --> 17:06.066
Those blunt ones,
are those your last ones?

17:07.234 --> 17:08.068
Yes...

17:08.777 --> 17:11.405
How many did the four of us kill?

17:11.822 --> 17:14.867
I don't know.
I didn't have the luxury to count.

17:15.868 --> 17:19.246
You know what?
I think I did a pretty good job myself.

17:20.414 --> 17:21.957
But the thing is...

17:23.167 --> 17:25.461
I wish I could have a drink before I go.

17:26.712 --> 17:27.546
Gelgar...

17:29.673 --> 17:31.216
Sorry, Nanaba.

17:32.217 --> 17:33.552
I must have hit my head...

17:34.261 --> 17:35.596
I can't hold...

17:36.722 --> 17:37.973
any longer...

17:39.516 --> 17:40.559
Gelgar!

17:53.363 --> 17:54.239
Gelgar!

17:55.699 --> 17:57.951
Damn it! Is that all I've got?

18:14.635 --> 18:15.677
Thank God.

18:35.405 --> 18:37.574
How cruel.

18:38.158 --> 18:39.576
This just isn't fair.

18:40.994 --> 18:44.081
Who the hell drank
the rest of this bottle?

18:50.546 --> 18:51.672
They got him.

18:53.882 --> 18:55.050
Quit it, Christa!

18:55.342 --> 18:57.886
The tower's about to crumble! You'll fall!

18:58.303 --> 19:00.430
But they're dying in our place!

19:00.681 --> 19:02.474
-Nanaba...
-No!

19:02.683 --> 19:03.976
-And Gelgar...
-No!

19:04.101 --> 19:06.145
Father, stop! Father!

19:06.478 --> 19:09.022
I'm sorry! I won't do it again!

19:09.314 --> 19:11.066
Father! No--

19:12.359 --> 19:13.777
Damn it all to hell!

19:14.486 --> 19:17.030
Hey, are we to wait here

19:17.156 --> 19:19.825
until the tower falls
and we get eaten alive?

19:20.784 --> 19:23.162
Isn't there anything we can do about it?

19:24.496 --> 19:25.539
This sucks...

19:25.956 --> 19:28.917
We'll be wiped out
without even finishing our mission.

19:32.171 --> 19:34.548
I want to keep fighting, too.

19:35.090 --> 19:40.053
If only I had some sort of weapon,
then I could fight and die alongside them.

19:40.304 --> 19:43.223
You're still saying things like that,
Christa?

19:44.600 --> 19:46.393
Don't you dare use their deaths.

19:46.768 --> 19:50.939
They didn't die so you'd have an excuse
to get yourself killed.

19:52.316 --> 19:54.735
That's not... That's not what I...

19:55.194 --> 19:57.613
You're not like Conny and the Scouts!

19:58.697 --> 20:00.991
They don't want to die,
but you don't even care.

20:01.783 --> 20:05.829
All you want to do is die in a way
that makes you seem like a hero.

20:06.288 --> 20:09.041
-That's not...
-Conny.

20:09.958 --> 20:13.503
-Give me that knife you have.
-What? My knife?

20:13.962 --> 20:16.256
-Just hand it over.
-Fine.

20:16.840 --> 20:17.674
Here.

20:20.677 --> 20:21.678
Thanks.

20:22.095 --> 20:23.764
What do you want it for?

20:24.264 --> 20:26.725
What? Well, you see...

20:29.061 --> 20:30.520
I'm going to fight this.

20:31.897 --> 20:33.815
What are you planning, Ymir?

20:34.358 --> 20:37.027
Who knows? I don't even know myself.

20:38.737 --> 20:39.571
Ymir...

20:41.365 --> 20:42.199
Christa.

20:43.408 --> 20:46.578
You've probably forgotten
all about it by now...

20:51.792 --> 20:54.294
But this might be the end, so...

20:55.003 --> 20:59.174
Try to remember that promise we made
while training on that snowy mountain.

21:02.261 --> 21:05.722
I have no right to tell you
how to live your life.

21:07.683 --> 21:11.561
So actually, this is nothing more
than a hope of mine...

21:13.689 --> 21:16.608
I want you to live a life you're proud of.

21:28.704 --> 21:30.330
Remember our promise, Christa.

21:32.708 --> 21:34.334
Ymir! Wait!

21:38.839 --> 21:39.965
Ymir!

23:28.698 --> 23:30.450
"Live a life you're proud of."

23:31.576 --> 23:35.956
Leaving Christa and those words behind,
Ymir unleashes the power of the Titans.

23:37.249 --> 23:42.546
Between Ymir and Christa is
a powerful promise they made in the past.

23:44.131 --> 23:46.466
As Ymir fights
and puts her life on the line,

23:46.842 --> 23:51.847
Christa screams out, casting aside
the persona she's kept for so long.

23:52.848 --> 23:55.809
Next episode, "Historia."
